# STATUS — cycle 8 / candidate A20 (2026-10-15)

Previous snapshot: `STATUS.md.cycle7-pre-A20`. Read
`INITRAMFS-DELIVERY-ROOT-CAUSE.md` first: it invalidates the standing assumption
that a BOOT-partition flash can change `/init` on this board.

## Headline (cycle 8)

**The reason nothing since A6 could be changed by flashing BOOT is now known and
fixed.** The S10+ bootloader advertises `/chosen/linux,initrd-start|end` to the
kernel **without populating that memory**, so the external ramdisk in `boot.img`
is always discarded (`rootfs image is not initramfs (junk in compressed archive)`
for BOTH lzma and gzip, with a correct delivered length). What actually runs is
the **initramfs embedded in the kernel image**. A7…A19 got their changes in only
because each of them rebuilt the kernel; A20 reused `Image-A19` and therefore ran
A19's `/init` for three consecutive flashes.

Fix: rebuild the kernel with `CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE=<the candidate cpio>`
(`tools/s10plus/a20/kbuild-a20.sh`, container `nuxel-kb`, ~1 min incremental).
`Image-A20` (48,781,320 B, sha256 `cdb974a8…`) carries the A20 initramfs.

